# README-First (Documentation Loading)

**Invoked by** [startup-session.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/startup-session.mdc) step 1. This rule defines **what to read** before coding. It does not replace the full startup ritual (scope, git, baseline, plan).

For project-specific facts (stack, commands, gaps), prefer [project-context.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/project-context.mdc) when the project has filled it in.

## Required Reads

| Priority | Document | When |
|----------|----------|------|
| 1 | Root `README.md` | Always |
| 2 | `ARCHITECTURE.md` or equivalent | If it exists |
| 3 | Service README (`frontend/`, `backend/`, etc.) | When that service is in scope |

## On-Demand Reads

Read when the task touches the area — do not load everything upfront:

| Task touches | Also read |
|--------------|-----------|
| Frontend routes, components, API calls | Frontend README + relevant `docs/` |
| Backend API, services, DB | Backend README + schema/migrations |
| Schema, migrations | Recent migration files + schema docs |
| Auth, permissions, multi-tenancy | Auth docs + middleware |
| Deployment, env, CI | Deploy docs + `.env.example` |

## While Working (not just at startup)

- **Code vs docs conflict** → verify code behavior first, update docs same session
- **Major changes** → trace impacted path across full data flow before editing
- **Terminology** → keep docs and code aligned
- **Completion** → don't mark done until docs reflect implemented behavior (see [documentation-maintenance.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/documentation-maintenance.mdc))

## README Delta Template

When recording changes in a changelog:

- **What changed** — one-line behavior description
- **Why** — bug fix / feature / refactor
- **Code touchpoints** — changed file paths
- **Data-flow impact** — which stages changed (or "none")
- **API / schema impact** — contract or migration changes (or "none")
- **Verification** — commands run + result
